@startuml
!include _style.puml
!include _sprites/postgresql.puml

title Container Diagram

skinparam nodesep 30
skinparam ranksep 55
skinparam ArrowFontSize 11
skinparam linetype polyline

' meshCoordinator: Headscale's own dedicated identity, modeled on how
' Certificate-Authority gets its own <<certAuthority>> stereotype rather
' than being lumped into <<infra>>. Headscale is third-party software, but
' it is still a component RAM-USB deploys and is responsible for (like CA)
' - unlike User-Client, which genuinely runs outside RAM-USB's control.
' Never mark Headscale <<external>>; it belongs inside the system boundary.
skinparam component<<meshCoordinator>> {
  BackgroundColor #4A7E9E/#345A73
  BorderColor #1F3E4E
  FontColor #F0F0F0
}

actor "User\n[Person]" as User
actor "Admin\n[Person]" as Admin

rectangle "RAM-USB System" {

  component "**Entry-Hub**\n[Go]\nPublic API gateway             " as EntryHub <<service>>
  component "**Security-Switch**\n[Go]\nRequest re-validation         " as SecuritySwitch <<service>>
  component "**Database-Vault**\n[Go]\nRe-validation, identity\nstorage & crypto" as DatabaseVault <<service>>
  component "**Storage-Service**\n[Go, SFTP]\nEncrypted backup storage" as StorageService <<service>>
  component "**Network-Manager**\n[Go]\nMesh & ACL orchestration" as NetworkManager <<service>>

  database "<$postgresql>\n**PostgreSQL**\nUser identity records" as Postgres

  component "**Certificate-Authority**\n[smallstep/certificates]\nmTLS issuance & rotation" as CA <<certAuthority>>
  component "**Headscale**\nMesh coordination server\n(own public VPS, NM-F-14)" as Headscale <<meshCoordinator>>
  component "**Observability**\n[Mosquitto, Metrics-Collector,\nGrafana, TimescaleDB]\nMetrics pipeline & dashboards" as Observability <<infra>>
}

' Headscale/Certificate-Authority positions swapped per user request:
' Headscale now sits top row (beside Entry-Hub), CA now sits where
' Headscale used to be (with Observability still anchored below it).
CA -[hidden]down-> Observability

' The two User->Entry-Hub HTTPS edges (public register/health, mesh-only
' login) are hand-drawn instead, in `draw-user-arrows-01.py` - parallel
' vertical lines landing on Entry-Hub's top edge at its first and third
' quarter marks, per explicit user request.
' User has NO remaining real edges (SFTP, Tailscale, and both HTTPS lines
' are all hand-drawn now) - without this hidden anchor, `dot` has nothing
' to rank User against and drifts it far from the RAM-USB System box.
User -[hidden]down-> EntryHub
EntryHub -down-> SecuritySwitch : **mTLS**
' SecuritySwitch->DatabaseVault and DatabaseVault->StorageService are
' hand-drawn instead, in `draw-mtls-chain-01.py`: PlantUML rendered them
' visibly oblique (their real x drifted several px along the path) despite
' EntryHub->SecuritySwitch, directly above, rendering perfectly vertical -
' per explicit user request, all three should share EntryHub-
' SecuritySwitch's own x. Kept as hidden edges here (not removed outright)
' so the vertical RANK ordering they provide doesn't disappear along with
' their visible line - same rationale as User's hidden anchor above.
SecuritySwitch -[hidden]down-> DatabaseVault
SecuritySwitch -[hidden]down-> DatabaseVault
DatabaseVault -right-> Postgres : **SQL**
DatabaseVault -[hidden]down-> StorageService
DatabaseVault -[hidden]down-> StorageService
SecuritySwitch -right-> NetworkManager : **mTLS**\nACL grant / pre-auth key
NetworkManager -[hidden]down- CA
' REST API (NetworkManager -> Headscale) is hand-drawn instead, in
' `draw-mtls-chain-01.py`: PlantUML renders this edge as an internal
' "back edge" (dot's own generated id literally reads "Headscale-backto-
' NetworkManager") since Headscale sits at a higher rank than
' NetworkManager despite the -up-> hint, and its tail didn't land on
' NetworkManager's true center - confirmed: 486.68 vs the box's actual
' center-x 491.0 - per explicit user report ("la punta della freccia e'
' nel posto giusto, ma la coda no"). Kept hidden here for the rank pull.
NetworkManager -[hidden]up-> Headscale

' SFTP (User -> Storage-Service) is deliberately NOT a PlantUML edge here:
' every attempt to route it under `dot` (norank+hint, plain ranked edge,
' invisible waypoint) either had no effect or triggered a full column
' reorder elsewhere in the diagram (see .claude/agent-memory/
' diagram-agent.md). It's hand-drawn instead, in the rendered SVG, by
' `draw-sftp-arrow-01.py` - same pattern as `center-legend-01.py` and
' 09-security-trust-zones.puml's `inject-cl-f-04-arc.py`.
' Tailscale coordination (User -> Headscale) is hand-drawn instead, in the
' rendered SVG, by `draw-user-arrows-01.py` - right angle from User's
' right side down into Headscale, per explicit user request. Same
' rationale as the SFTP arrow above: PlantUML/dot routing control over
' individual edge shape/side is unreliable in this file without side
' effects elsewhere.

Observability <-right- Admin : **HTTPS**\ndashboards

legend
  Entry-Hub exposes two listeners (EH-F-03): register/health are public (solid arrow);
  login is mesh-only (dashed arrow) and reachable only after the User to Headscale mesh join (CL-F-04).
end legend

@enduml
